  title: Chinese New Year - 19th Century
  info: 'Brought to Singapore by Chinese immigrants, Lunar New Year became a major
    celebration marked by family reunions, lion dances, red packets, and symbolic
    foods. It reflects the deep-rooted cultural traditions of the Chinese community
    and their integration into Singaporean society.  '
